## 6. The design residual
979:1. **Scheduled automation stays unexplained.** An execution with a `schedule` trigger (for example `kpi.reporting_period_open`, the `*_scan` starters, the engine ticks) has no journalled cause. If one runs on T between the import and D9, its rows, and the rows its job writes, are `unexplained`, and mode 2 exits 4. Explaining them would mean explaining rows by the scheduler, not by the drill's 
980-   - DO-D4 reports any such row as a FAIL with its key and trigger code;
981-   - DO-D4 never pauses, disables or reschedules a job to avoid it, because that would also change `job_schedule`, which B.6 job-check pins;
982-   - the orchestrator decides.
983-
984-   T-B17 measured none in its window (DO-D3 handback finding 3).
985-2. **The same-transaction link is a timestamp equality.** PostgreSQL stores no transaction id per row. Two transactions that start in the same microsecond, write an outbox row and an explained event on the **same aggregate**, would be indistinguishable. Both events would still be on that record, so the record touched is right either way.
docs/architecture/p7-work-split.md:1597:- A scheduled automation row that lands in the window (A3.9 residual 1) is a FAIL with its key and trigger code. Never pause, disable or reschedule a job to avoid it. Report it, and the orchestrator decides.
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-ARCH-R4-solution-architect.md:65:- **The escalation condition is not met.** The one case that would meet it, scheduled automation that lands in the drill window, is kept **unexplained** (A3.9 residual 1). DO-D4 reports it if it happens and must not pause the schedul
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-ARCH-R4-solution-architect.md:97:2. **Scheduled automation in the drill window stays unexplained** (A3.9 residual 1). If T-B11 hits it, T-B11 FAILs and the orchestrator decides. I did not pre-authorize any loosening.
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D4-devops-engineer.md:106:5. **No scheduled automation row** (A3.9 residual 1) appeared in T-B17's window. Mode 2 matched.

