## Conclusion
On candidate 07af9fba the shipped A18 drill (deploy/scripts/transfer-drill.sh) and the A18 harness (tests/qa/integration/a18-transfer-drill.test.ts) FAIL at D9 whenever approval.escalation_scan (starter.decision_sla, schedule trigger, */15 Asia/Riyadh) runs on the target between D7 and D9. The product behaves correctly (a scheduled job runs after a restart; its execution and audit are written); the mode 2 recheck classifies the schedule-triggered execution as unexplained by design (ADR-0064 A3.9 residual 1). The result of the A18 acceptance drill therefore depends on the wall clock: 2 of my 5 D9 runs on this candidate failed (run-1 harness at 07:15, repro attempt 2 at 08:00) and 3 passed (run-1 direct, run-2 harness, repro attempt 1; none of their windows contained a quarter hour). The residual is recorded in ADR-0064 and p7-work-split only. It is not in known-limitations.md, the release notes, the deployment guide or the A18 register rows (REQ-S19-017, REQ-S20-018, REQ-S01-006), and decisions.md holds no orchestrator decision on it (A3.9: 'the orchestrator decides').
